{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"inferior-seaborgium-aruanas","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nTeams plan and ship work by release in Jira, using the issue field `fixVersions`. rebar has no release concept, so the bridge drops that field:\n- The reconciler's field contract (`src/rebar/reconciler/_field_contract.py`) registers 11 fields: status, links, parent, title, assignee, priority, type, description, comments, labels and watchers. Nothing in `src/rebar` reads `fixVersions`.\n- Compiled ticket state (`src/rebar/reducer/_state.py`) has no release field.\n- No CLI, MCP or library surface can show, filter or set a release.\n\nSo an agent or person working from rebar can't answer \"what is in release X?\" or \"which release is this ticket targeted at?\" without going back to Jira. Release membership is also invisible to `next-batch` and `ready`, and to metrics.\n\n## Goal\n\nMake release a first-class rebar ticket field, and sync it from Jira's `fixVersions` into rebar through the existing reconciler. Once a bridged ticket's fix version changes in Jira, the next reconcile pass shows that change in `rebar show`, in `list` filters, and in the MCP read tools.\n\n## Approach\n\nFollow the shape of existing fields; don't add a parallel subsystem.\n\n1. **ADR first.** Record the design under `docs/adr/`. It must cover:\n   - the field's shape;\n   - the replayed event that carries it (prefer `EDIT.fields`, which replay already merges last-wins, over a new event type);\n   - its symmetry class in `FIELD_CONTRACT`;\n   - how Jira version identity maps to rebar (version `id` versus `name`, and renames);\n   - what happens when a Jira version is archived or deleted.\n2. **Store and reducer.** Add the field to compiled state with a default, and compact it into `SNAPSHOT`. Older stores replay unchanged, and older readers ignore the field under the schema forward-compatibility rules in `docs/event-schema.md`.\n3. **Reconciler inbound.**\n   - Fetch `fixVersions` for bridged issues in both Jira adapters (Cloud and Data Center, through the `jira_family` seam, ADR 0055).\n   - Translate the field in `inbound_translate.py` / `inbound_fields.py`, and diff it in `inbound_differ.py`.\n   - Apply it through `apply_inbound_events`.\n   - Register it in `FIELD_CONTRACT` and `conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES`, so the contract property tests cover it.\n4. **Surfaces.**\n   - `rebar show`, the `list` / `search` filters, and the MCP read tools expose the field. Their `outputSchema`s and `docs/mcp-reference.md` are updated.\n   - The public-API surface census is updated deliberately.\n5. **Docs.** Update `docs/event-schema.md`, `docs/ticket-model.md`, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md`, and the reconciler record ADR 0121 where field coverage is enumerated.\n\n## Design questions to settle in the ADR (each one changes the children's plans)\n\n- **Cardinality.** Jira allows several fix versions per issue. Either keep a list, mirroring Jira, or keep a single value and define which wins.\n- **Direction.** The request is Jira→rebar sync. Decide whether rebar can edit the field locally, and whether local edits push to Jira. That decides inbound-only versus a bidirectional or one-way-gated symmetry class. The contract has no inbound-only class today.\n- **Release as an entity.** Either store only the release name on the ticket, or also keep release records (Jira version id, name, released flag, release date) that rebar can list on their own.\n- **Affects versions.** Jira's separate `versions` field (affected versions) is out of scope unless the ADR brings it in.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- **Portability.** Works with any or no CI provider. A store with no Jira bridge has the field empty, and every command behaves as before.\n- **No config key.** A bridged project needs no new setting. The field syncs whenever the bridge runs. Any new mechanism needs a marker that names an open sunset ticket under this epic.\n- **Module size.** The 800-line cap, complexity ratchet and mechanism ratchet stay green. Split along existing seams; don't grow near-cap reconciler modules.\n- **No drift on old tickets.** Existing bridged tickets must not churn: a first pass over an unchanged store writes only the new field's initial values. A repeat pass writes nothing.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] An ADR under `docs/adr/` records the field shape, event carrier, symmetry class, Jira version identity mapping, and archived/deleted version handling. Each design question above is answered there.\n- [ ] Compiled ticket state carries the release field, with an empty default. `SNAPSHOT` compaction preserves it, and replaying an existing store unchanged yields an empty value for every ticket. Pinned by reducer and compaction tests.\n- [ ] A reconcile pass that sees a bridged Jira issue's `fixVersions` change writes the matching rebar event. A repeat pass with no Jira change writes nothing. Pinned for both the Jira Cloud and Data Center adapters by tests over recorded API payloads.\n- [ ] The field is registered in `FIELD_CONTRACT` and `conflict_resolver.FIELD_CLASSES`, and the contract property tests pass for it.\n- [ ] `rebar show` displays the field. `rebar list` can filter by release. The MCP read tools return it in their declared `outputSchema`. Pinned by CLI, MCP and library tests.\n- [ ] `docs/event-schema.md`, `docs/ticket-model.md`, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` and `docs/mcp-reference.md` describe the field. The doc-drift tests pass.\n- [ ] A store with no Jira bridge passes the existing test suite unchanged.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the final child's merge.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] On the production bridge, after deploy, one REB issue's fix version set in Jira appears on its bound rebar ticket after the next reconcile pass. Shown with `rebar show`, and recorded in a ticket comment with the pass time.","id":"21ec-3e9b-4a27-4775","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"epic","title":"Sync Jira fix versions into rebar as a first-class release field"},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1793912050029097001,"uuid":"6dc719bf-d232-44e9-bcb3-dcd5630b2a5d"}